Now I see a critical issue! In `present_target_choice`, when `targets.len() == 1 && !optional`:

```rust
if targets.len() == 1 && !optional {
    // Mandatory with exactly 1 target — auto-apply.
    let reg = crate::cards::CardRegistry::with_all_cards();
    crate::engine::apply_pending_effect(state, &targets[0], &effect, &reg);
    return;
}
```

This creates a NEW `CardRegistry::with_all_cards()` rather than using the one passed in. This might be a minor issue but probably works correctly in practice.


The `creature_targets` function gathers all creatures on the battlefield, including Morkrut Banshee itself, so the Banshee can target itself as the ruling allows. When the Banshee is the only creature and morbid is active, the function returns just that one target, triggering the auto-apply logic since `targets.len() == 1 && !optional` is true—which correctly implements the ruling that the ability must target the Banshee itself if no other creatures exist.

I'm also verifying that the engine properly clears the `until_end_of_turn_effects` at the end of turn cleanup, which I can see it does in the code.

Now I need to check how `effective_power` and `effective_toughness` actually apply these temporary effects to the creature stats.

